{"title":"2001 IMO Shortlist Problems/N6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#First_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">First Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Second_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Second Solution</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/N6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Is it possible to find 100 positive integers not exceeding 25,000, such that all pairwise sums of them are different?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/N6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The answer is yes.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"First_Solution\">First Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/N6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: First Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For example, let's say that the integers are, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/5/16591137687b5cd7197f2346d0b0d554595d3f16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k, k+a_1, k+a_2, ..., k+a_{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"210\" height=\"16\" />. Now this turns into a problem of solving for the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a313bf06349648df7be807bee95b651604ce7a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />. This then each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> takes on the form, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/b/44b09b6eb471e7d55ca0f07f5b64d7ae7ce8418f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j+b_1, j+b_2,..., j+b_{98}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"183\" height=\"16\" />. Then we must find the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/1/73119f04d6ae5f6eb4afc8c9c946a5744a11be50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$98$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> integers. By doing this process over and over again, we obtain the last <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/b/40ba633daa12c45e60ba09e51bab056b7f5eabd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y, y+u_1, y+u_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"123\" height=\"14\" />. Obviously these 3 integers can have different sums, and the number of different \"parts\" in every sequence (the number of terms that are different for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/2/b22c47698a8e2650b50c8b700823716c662e58c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i, b_i, c_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" />, etc.) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d8bc940412e77a439fecb416a50b7492fdf3fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99+98+\\ldots+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"132\" height=\"14\" />, not exceeding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/b/65ba6fa952e48e67613a0abcc5fd9b41f6a15b2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25000$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Second_Solution\">Second Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/N6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Second Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><b>Lemma:</b> We try to show that for a prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, there are such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> integers less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/9/5191a9eec04f5b50cfe27ba85c60088856f14f44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2p^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" />. Then it suffices because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/a/f9ae10b6854fdc733ac2e488fbe440dce59887b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=101&gt;100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"112\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/0/f4079ecf66c2c28827bd7c232f29c8ec7be94f70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot 101^2&lt;25000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"125\" height=\"15\" /> is enough.\n</p><p><i>Proof:</i> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/1/0d14bd6098f30372484079834c7fc89bed1be10d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"2\" />Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/a/4da917b79ef5b4e5e52b28dea7fddde35cbd18ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bar a$\" width=\"9\" height=\"10\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/8/f88716db5e37bfe7a87b9f23c3cc06e8d3220ddb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2\\equiv \\bar a\\bmod p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/4/1f4fd4c5df121b8fffeef9fc26ea17490e4380d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\hat i=2pi+\\bar i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"20\" />. Then, we show that the integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/1/ba10074e15c38c8ae6f29c4938e9e4565b0abc5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\hat i$\" width=\"5\" height=\"16\" /> does the trick for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50ed4b89a6aeb4814026a2be01bde8bd7d264b71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/d/04d30e49d2dbcfcd12b704fc51fac648788b392e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\hat a+\\hat b\\equiv \\hat c+\\hat d\\pmod p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"174\" height=\"22\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e65b5ccb45f03ee887c4c834e6a310286751cbbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(a+b)p+\\bar a+\\bar b\\equiv 2(c+d)p+\\bar c+\\bar d\\pmod p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"362\" height=\"20\" />. Thus, we may say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/a/baa6f49f09f17d874b3ac49fc483f40cfb54bd00.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a+b\\equiv c+d\\pmod p\\qquad (\\dag)\\]\" width=\"239\" height=\"18\" /> and, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acccf5b965c76881adf6cd16195c3cee329adf31.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\bar a+\\bar b\\equiv \\bar c+\\bar d\\pmod p\\qquad(*)\\]\" width=\"240\" height=\"20\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/3/e1325125a37507c0b2aca029f801c5b68be3ce34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bar a&lt;p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />. From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf3ac1ec5c42da2289f5bc9764045a980f5b3673.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\dag)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/0/290208646d17db217114feeca9d8bd8df856fc9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\equiv c+d-b\\pmod p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"174\" height=\"18\" />. From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/0/9d02e715e7f7195675151570530c5b62ba7b2744.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(*)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />, we infer that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/d/c6d553968100e196ccb97015d8924299e49f75d9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2+b^2\\equiv c^2+d^2\\pmod p\\]\" width=\"213\" height=\"19\" /> which gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/3/a7394ba30e1ef7075c93e2594500cd8fd5077865.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(c+d-b)^2+b^2\\equiv c^2+d^2\\pmod p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"281\" height=\"21\" />. Factorizing, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/1/cc1b2ebeff6654ab88a32b3063ca85ed25cbfffd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(b^2-bc-bd+cd)\\equiv0\\pmod p\\]\" width=\"269\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/b/f2b9ead8b8906270b93bca564079d22f42523e82.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies(b-c)(b-d)\\equiv0\\pmod p\\]\" width=\"258\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>This yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/9/949e0692e9de82c604f7695fa494e2169e9577ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p|b-c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/5/585238f8bf4bf470aae21753c77dfd624ec48c3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p|b-d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />. But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/0/540e521f86a72bbb9abe59d34756b0c8c223228c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|b-c|&lt;p\\implies b=c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"171\" height=\"18\" />, and this implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/5/4d595f9f37a3da73bbbe5b087d6ec2c78435a402.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />. The other case is similar. So, we are done.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, every sum must be distinct, as desired.\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/N6&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/N6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems\" title=\"2001 IMO Shortlist Problems\">2001 IMO Shortlist Problems</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t=17475\">Discussion on AOPS/MathLinks</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018045200\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.024 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.040 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 226/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 353/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7402/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.194      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n100.00%    6.194      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7202:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018045200 and revision id 291178. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}